      "gitCommitMessage": "Fix QA sweep findings: sync chunking, outbox write race, encrypted session; bump to 1.2.4 (226)\n\n- api.ts/store.ts: chunk sync() into MAX_SYNC_BATCH (2000) requests so a\n  shift's queue past the server's per-request cap keeps draining instead\n  of retrying one oversized, permanently-rejected payload forever.\n- db.ts: serialize saveOutbox through a chained/coalescing queue instead\n  of firing an unawaited write per scan, which could interleave two\n  non-exclusive SQLite transactions and lose a row.\n- secure-storage.ts (new): SecureStore-backed encrypted adapter for the\n  Supabase session (random AES key in SecureStore, encrypted blob in\n  AsyncStorage - avoids SecureStore's ~2048-byte value cap). Wired into\n  api.ts in place of the raw AsyncStorage storage adapter. New deps:\n  expo-crypto, aes-js, @types/aes-js.\n- app.json: version 1.2.3 -> 1.2.4, runtimeVersion likewise (expo-crypto\n  is a new native module, so a future OTA under the old runtime could\n  crash a phone built before this change - see the comment in the file),\n  iOS buildNumber 225 -> 226, Android versionCode 225 -> 226.\n\nVerified: tsc --noEmit clean, full npm test green (12 suites, no\nfailures) both before and after.",
