      "gitCommitHash": "d1fa7d49f3c1e9f881d4cad08c96b7dcaa6cf9c2",
      "gitCommitMessage": "Fix dead duplicate-scan tick on the Ship/Return loop\n\nFull line-by-line comparison against the legacy scanner turned up a\nsecond bug beyond autofocus: scan.tsx tracked its own 2.5s cooldown to\ngive one light haptic tick the first time a held-still barcode gets\nsuppressed (A SILENT COOLDOWN IS A CAMERA THAT LOOKS DEAD), but\nScanner already suppresses the repeat read at the same 2.5s duration\nbefore take() is ever called again -- so that branch could never run.\nThe intended still alive tick had never once fired.\n\nAdded onDuplicate to Scanner, called from deliver() whenever a read is\nsuppressed by cooldown, and wired scan.tsx's tick logic to it instead\nof a redundant, unreachable check of its own.",
      "priority": "HIGH",
      "createdAt": "2026-08-18T18:48:57.917Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-08-18T18:53:33.167Z",
      "completedAt": "2026-08-18T18:53:32.841Z",
