      "gitCommitHash": "4da030c66a4a1889d4fb413ad4814ddf7f0ccf1a",
      "gitCommitMessage": "Stop Sentry's source-map upload failing the build\n\nAdding the Sentry Expo config plugin switched on source-map upload as a build step, and that step runs sentry-cli, which needs an auth token nobody has created: 'Auth token is required for this request.' The upload failing took the whole iOS build down with it. That is my doing - the plugin went in to make stack traces readable and I did not account for what it turns on.\n\nSENTRY_DISABLE_AUTO_UPLOAD=true on all three profiles. Crash reporting is unaffected - errors still reach Sentry with full context. What is lost is the symbolication step, so a stack trace names a minified chunk rather than a line of our code. Worth having, not worth a build that cannot ship.\n\nTO GET IT BACK: create a token in Sentry under Settings > Auth Tokens with the project:releases scope, add it with 'eas secret:create --scope project --name SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN --value <token>', and drop this variable. The secret belongs in EAS rather than in this file - unlike the DSN, an auth token is a real credential.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GNaDGKQ8eDYZXmfhCw3ZNr",
      "priority": "NORMAL",
      "createdAt": "2026-08-11T04:11:51.021Z",
